From b50ee1bbcf0cd6ac9d139398d3a4907208c3a0ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:35:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Match 128-row vocab head tile pipeline stages

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 2756478b60b90700b9918b457aeb38657da637b5.

Rationale:
In vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/vocab.py, TILE_CONFIGS[128] used num_stages=4 with act_stages=2 so four 32x128 weight stages and two 128x128 activation stages fit under the 99 KiB GB10 shared-memory ceiling (98,304 B). However, offsetting activation staging (stage 2) from weight cp.async staging (stage 0) inside T.Pipelined(..., stage=[2, 0, 0, 3, 3]) causes TileLang to emit three unrolled pipeline drain blocks with three simultaneously live bfloat16_t A_local[32] register arrays across cp.async_wait<3/2/1/0> barriers. That inflated register pressure on SM121 from 86 registers (block_M=64) to 195 registers in packed_vocab_projection and 197 registers in packed_vocab_greedy_partials (50,432 registers/CTA at 256 threads), making the 128-row tile at M=128 slower than launching two waves of the 64-row tile on both TP4 (N=32320) and TP3 (N=43136).

Setting TILE_CONFIGS[128] to num_stages=2 (matching activation and weight pipeline depth at stage=[0, 0, 0, 1, 1]) reduces dynamic shared memory from 98,304 B to 86,016 B (78,336 B for NVFP4), eliminates two unrolled drain stages, and cuts register allocation from 195 to 97 registers in packed_vocab_projection and from 197 to 100 registers in packed_vocab_greedy_partials with zero spills. Across M=72..128 in captured CUDA graphs on GB10, this speeds up packed_vocab_projection and packed_vocab_greedy_partials by up to 10.2% (-195.8 us at M=128) on TP4 and up to 11.5% (-280.4 us at M=128) on TP3.

Quality:
Bit-identical (torch.equal) FP32 and BF16 logits and greedy (max, index) pairs across all M=1..128 on TP4 and TP3 shards; identical K accumulation order and tile reduction tree.

Tests:
- pytest tests/kernels/quantization/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_vocab.py tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_pdl.py tests/v1/worker/gpu/test_greedy_verification.py (105 passed across 2 boots).

Upstream status: local TileLang SM121 vocabulary head pipeline tuning.
---
